  "physical_design_rules": [
    "Use stable surrogate IDs, plus unique source identities and conservative normalized-URL SHA256 values. Compare actual normalized strings on hash conflict.",
    "Use binary/case-sensitive URL storage; preserve meaningful path/query differences and do not collapse hosts or redirects without evidence.",
    "Store timestamps in UTC with source value and precision; preserve date-only values. Crawl/import/file timestamps must not become page lastmod.",
    "Retain NULL for unknown metadata. Empty alt text means explicitly decorative and is distinct from unknown alt text.",
    "Image/video bytes stay in existing object storage. Store locations, metadata, hashes and relationships in SQL.",
    "Use typed, indexed columns for frequently queried fields and relationships; JSON for sparse descriptive extensions and raw evidence.",
    "Index both directions of relationships: page/asset, source/target, parent/variant; index eligibility channel/decision, canonical host/module and import/version.",
    "Every rendered_rendition_id in media_uses must belong to the same asset_id; enforce in the importer and with appropriate composite references where supported.",
    "Keep original-file identity, logical artwork identity, byte equality and rendition identity separate. Never merge distinct artwork solely because one thumbnail hash matches.",
    "Store actual placements separately from planned semantic relationships; planned care links must not be counted as deployed internal links.",
    "Manage evidence as content/version changes and referenced import artifacts rather than repeating entire unchanged crawl dumps in database rows.",
    "Use database foreign-key constraints where compatible and enabled. Verify existing PlanetScale settings before preparing executable DDL; do not change settings from this proposal."
  ],
